syntax = behavior

Feature: "Flashcard Insights Dashboard"

    Note: [[
    As a User
    I want to view my estimated knowledge metrics, predictive review forecasts, streaks, multipliers, and coin allocations
    So that I can understand my learning velocity, memory stability, upcoming workloads, and financial gains
    ]]

    Diagram: "FSRS Memory Pipeline & Insights" [[
    graph TD
        A[Card Grading History] --> B[FSRS Scheduling Engine]
        B --> C[Active Knowledge Estimation]
        B --> D[Memory Stability Curve]
        B --> E[Ease Factor Distribution]
        B --> F[30-Day Review Forecast]
        B --> G[Card Status Breakdown]
        A --> H[Wallet Earnings Audit]
    ]]

    Background: "Revision Data Context"
        Given "the user has active flashcards with revision history data"
        And "the user navigates to the Flashcard Analytics Dashboard view"

    Rule: "Summary metrics track real-time memory strength, recall probability, and gamification status"

        Scenario: "Displaying core knowledge retention metrics"
            Then "the dashboard displays the \"Active Knowledge\" metric representing the estimated amount of information recallable at this moment"
            And "the dashboard displays the \"Success Rate\" metric providing a real-time prediction of execution performance"
            And "the dashboard displays the \"Retention Rate\" metric measuring the average retrievability across all learned cards"

        Scenario: "Displaying revision streaks and active coin multipliers"
            Then "the dashboard displays the user's current flashcard revision session streak"
            And "the dashboard displays the active coin multiplier applied to earnings"

    Rule: "Economy verification ensures flashcard study actions reward the user"

        Scenario: "Confirming wallet credit deposits for successful revisions"
            Then "the dashboard displays the total coins earned specifically via flashcard active recall"
            And "the balance reflects that each completed study loop successfully credited the wallet according to economic configurations"

    Rule: "Visual profiles map out collection complexity and historical progression"

        Scenario: "Viewing the collection complexity profile"
            Then "the dashboard displays an \"Ease Factor Distribution\" chart"
            And "the chart visualizes the difficulty and complexity variance across the flashcard library"

        Scenario: "Evaluating long-term memory strength"
            Then "the dashboard displays a \"Memory Stability\" chart"
            And "the chart represents the absolute durability of the user's long-term memory tracks"

        Scenario: "Forecasting future revision workloads"
            Then "the dashboard displays a \"30-Day Review Forecast\" chart"
            And "the chart calculates exactly when each card in the collection will next become due over the upcoming month"

        Scenario: "Visualizing card lifecycle states"
            Then "the dashboard displays a \"Card Status Distribution\" chart"
            And "the chart provides a breakdown of where cards currently reside within the learning process lifecycle"